Figure 2 CVs of the different modified electrode at \(100\;\mathrm{mV/s}\) in \(5\;\mathrm{mM}\;[\mathrm{Fe}(\mathrm{CN})_{6}]^{3-/4-}\) solution : (a) bare GCE, (b) AuNPs/GCE, (c) HP2/AuNPs/GCE (d) HT/HP2/AuNPs/GCE, (e) s2 (s2')/HT/HP2/AuNPs/GCE.

Optimization of detection conditions

The test conditions such as the concentration of \(\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}_{2}\), the \(\mathrm{pH}\) of solution and the reaction time of recycle process were investigated by the aptasensor with \(10\;\mathrm{nM}\) TB as a model. Firstly, the concentration of \(\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}_{2}\) in testing buffer solution plays an important role in this strategy. To investigate the effect of \(\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}_{2}\) concentration, the aptasensor was detected in PBS solution \((\mathrm{pH}\ 7.0)\) with different concentration of
\(\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}_{2}\) (from \(1.69\,\mathrm{mM}\) to \(3.68\,\mathrm{mM}\)). In Figure 3A, with the concentration of \(\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}_{2}\) increased, the peak current increased and became stable at \(3.21\,\mathrm{mM}\), suggesting the highest electrocatalytic efficiency at this point. Therefore, \(3.21\,\mathrm{mM}\) of \(\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}_{2}\) was selected throughout the whole experiment.

In this work, the fabricated aptasensor was detected in PBS buffer with different pH value. In Figure 3B, from 5.0 to 7.0, the current increased with the pH value increased firstly and then decreased after the pH value was larger than 7.0. Therefore, the value of 7.0 for the working buffer was adopted for the investigation.

The reaction time of recycle process was studied from \(20\,\mathrm{min}\) to \(140\,\mathrm{min}\). From the results indicated in Figure 3C, we can see the peak current increased when the recycle time achieved to \(120\,\mathrm{min}\), where a maximum current was obtained. After 120 min, the peak current has no obvious change. Therefore, the optimal reaction time of recycle process was chosen as \(120\,\mathrm{min}\).

